 debt): THE TRIPWIRE FOR OLD, CORRECTED SENTENCES IS WIDENED IN FIVE WAYS.

THE FIVE, as main's table gives them, each made again on the tripwire's own reader before it was mended:

1. NO OLD FORM FOR ONE FINDING. E11 had none. Its sentence is the one this arc's table quotes: that the sine of a seventh of pi has no radical closed form. It is looked for now, and its correction must name the radicals.
2. TREES THAT WERE NOT READ. The tripwire listed three folders and eight root pages: no script outside an arc, no test and no page of the other trees was read. Every tracked file is listed now. Two things are history and are said to be: the progress log, which is append-only, and a harvested copy of another branch's sweep of the changelog's history. With them set aside the wider reading reports nothing on the tree.
3. A MARK THAT ACCEPTS AN UNCORRECTED CLAIM. The mark for E8 was one word, read in any case, so a sentence that states the claim and names the embedding in passing was taken as corrected. The mark is the correction's own words now, with its capitals. WHICH MARK THE READER FOUND IS NOT KNOWN TO THE BUILDER: its file is read through a mask and main's planted pages were not in its folder. This is the one found here.
4. A CUE IN A LATER QUOTED PARAGRAPH. A quotation of several paragraphs was one block, so a cue in a later paragraph excused the claim in an earlier one. A line that holds the mark of quotation and nothing else parts two blocks now, as an empty line does.
5. A FORM IN BOLD. A word of the old form set in bold, in italics or as code hid the form. The marks of emphasis are taken out before the forms are looked for.

THE PLANTED CASES, in the patch's own test: nine pages, each an old form with no correction, and four twins that carry one. They are the builder's, written from main's descriptions. As the tripwire stood, it reported none of the nine: 7 it did not read or found no form in, and 2 it took as corrected. It reports the nine now, and none of the twins.

NOT CLOSED, as before and as the lock says: the correction's words added to a sentence that still asserts the claim; a rewording outside the spellings listed (register row P-817).

The lock: 14 tests pass. Every gate passes but the count of landings. 0 of 19.
